note        the reduce tuple changed shape, deliberately
    `__reduce__` returns (class, (), state) now rather than (class, (17 args)). A pickle written before this tip still loads here -- no third element, no __setstate__ call, the old constructor path. A pickle written here needs the new __setstate__, because the default unpickling path would put every Reaction field in the instance dictionary where the class's descriptor shadows it. RMG pickles reactions within a run (multiprocessing, deepcopy), not across versions, so this is stated rather than worked around.

